.TH GFP 1 "September 2026" "gfp-cli 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
gfp \- Git-compatible CLI layer and command wrapper for Perforce Helix Core (p4)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B gfp
[\fB\-h\fR | \fB\-\-help\fR]
.br
.B gfp
\fIsubcommand\fR [\fIoptions\fR] [\fIarguments\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B gfp
is a modular, extensible command-line wrapper that translates standard Git workflows, mental models, and lifecycle hooks into native Perforce Helix Core (\fBp4\fR) operations. It enables software engineers familiar with Git to interact seamlessly with Perforce repositories without sacrificing native Perforce capabilities such as changelists, streams, and server-side shelving.

.B gfp
requires zero server-side modifications or background daemons. It operates directly as an intelligent client layer over the standard Perforce CLI (\fBp4\fR).

.SS Workspace Root Resolution
When invoked,
.B gfp
resolves the active workspace root in the following precedence order:
.IP 1. 4
A directory in the current working directory hierarchy containing a \fB.gfp\fR marker directory.
.IP 2. 4
The \fBClient root:\fR directory reported by \fBp4 info\fR.
.IP 3. 4
The current working directory (\fIcwd\fR) as a fallback.

.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
.BR status ", " st
Display the workspace state, including opened files (add, edit, delete), untracked unreconciled files, active client workspace, and pending changelists.
.RS
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-cl ", " \-\-pending
Display all numbered pending changelists associated with the workspace, including both opened and shelved files.
.RE

.TP
.BR add
Stage/open files in the Perforce client workspace for add, edit, or delete via \fBp4 reconcile\fR.
.RS
.TP
.BR \-A ", " \-\-all
Stage all modifications and untracked files across the entire workspace.
.TP
.BR \-u ", " \-\-update
Stage modified and deleted files only, ignoring untracked files.
.RE

.TP
.BR commit ", " ci
Create a new numbered pending changelist with a commit description, or amend an existing changelist. See \fBgfp\-commit\fR(1).
.RS
.TP
.BR \-m " " \fIMESSAGE\fR ", " \-\-message " " \fIMESSAGE\fR
Changelist description text.
.TP
.BR \-a ", " \-\-all
Automatically reconcile and stage all workspace changes before committing.
.TP
.B \-\-amend
Update the description or file list of an existing pending changelist.
.TP
.BR \-c " " \fICL\fR ", " \-\-cl " " \fICL\fR
Target pending changelist ID to amend.
.RE

.TP
.BR diff ", " di
Show unified diff of modified files in the workspace against the depot head revision.
.RS
.TP
.BR \-c " " \fICL\fR ", " \-\-cl " " \fICL\fR
Display diffs for files within a specific pending or submitted changelist ID.
.TP
.B \-\-stat
Generate a diffstat histogram summarizing added, modified, and deleted lines per file.
.TP
.BR \-\-color "[=\fIWHEN\fR]"
Show colored diff. \fIWHEN\fR can be \fBalways\fR, \fBnever\fR, or \fBauto\fR (default: auto).
.TP
.B \-\-no\-color
Turn off colored diff output (equivalent to \fB\-\-color=never\fR).
.RE

.TP
.BR log
Display submitted changelist history in reverse chronological order.
.RS
.TP
.BR \-n " " \fICOUNT\fR ", " \-\-max\-count " " \fICOUNT\fR
Limit output to the specified number of changelists (default: 30).
.TP
.BR \-a ", " \-\-all
Display full changelist descriptions without truncation.
.TP
.B \-\-oneline
Display compact one-line log format (<CL> <author> <date> <summary>).
.TP
.BR \-p ", " \-\-patch
Display inline unified diff patches for each listed changelist.
.TP
.BR \-u " " \fIUSER\fR ", " \-\-user " " \fIUSER\fR ", " \-\-author " " \fIUSER\fR
Filter history by changelist author.
.RE

.TP
.BR pull
Sync latest depot revisions to the workspace and automatically merge non-conflicting edits (\fBp4 sync\fR followed by \fBp4 resolve \-am\fR).
.RS
.TP
.BR \-f ", " \-\-force
Force resynchronization of all workspace files from the depot (\fBp4 sync \-f\fR).
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-dry\-run
Preview files that would be updated without transferring data from the server.
.RE

.TP
.BR push
Submit changelists to the depot. By default, shelves the changelist to trigger Jenkins gated CI submit queue validation, or directly submits with \fB\-f\fR. See \fBgfp\-push\fR(1).
.RS
.TP
.BR \-c " " \fICL\fR ", " \-\-cl " " \fICL\fR
Specific pending changelist ID to push (defaults to the most recent pending changelist).
.TP
.BR \-f ", " \-\-force
Bypass the Jenkins gated submit queue and submit directly to the depot (\fBp4 submit\fR).
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-dry\-run
Preview push actions without shelving or submitting.
.TP
.B \-\-gated
Explicitly request submission via the Jenkins gated submit queue (default behavior).
.RE

.TP
.BR checkout ", " co
Discard local modifications to opened files by reverting them to the depot head revision (\fBp4 revert\fR).
.RS
.TP
.BR \-f ", " \-\-force
Reconcile unopened local changes into opened edits first before reverting.
.RE

.TP
.BR stash
Shelve or unshelve working changes to/from the Perforce server.
.RS
.TP
.B save
Shelve currently opened files into a pending changelist and revert the local workspace files.
.TP
.B pop
Unshelve files from a shelved changelist into the workspace and delete the server-side shelf.
.TP
.B list
List all shelved changelists associated with the current client workspace or user.
.TP
.B drop
Delete shelved files from a changelist on the Perforce server (\fBp4 shelve \-d\fR).
.TP
.B show
Display files and unified diffs of a shelved changelist.
.TP
.BR \-m " " \fIMESSAGE\fR ", " \-\-message " " \fIMESSAGE\fR
Stash description note.
.TP
.BR \-c " " \fICL\fR ", " \-\-cl " " \fICL\fR
Specify target changelist ID for stash operations.
.TP
.BR \-k ", " \-\-keep
Keep local workspace modifications intact after shelving during \fBstash save\fR.
.RE

.TP
.BR show
Display full changelist metadata, affected files, and unified diffs for a submitted or shelved changelist (\fBp4 describe \-du\fR).
.RS
.TP
.BR \-s ", " \-\-stat
Show summary of modified files without full diff contents.
.RE

.TP
.BR clean
Remove untracked and unreconciled files from the workspace directory tree (\fBp4 clean\fR).
.RS
.TP
.BR \-f ", " \-\-force
Execute file deletions without interactive confirmation.
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-dry\-run
Preview files that would be removed without deleting anything.
.TP
.B \-d
Recursively delete empty untracked directories.
.RE

.TP
.BR blame
Annotate each line of a file with revision numbers, changelist IDs, authors, and dates (\fBp4 annotate\fR).
.RS
.TP
.BR \-c " " \fICL\fR ", " \-\-cl " " \fICL\fR ", " \-\-rev " " \fIREV\fR
Annotate file as of a specific changelist ID or revision number.
.TP
.BR \-u ", " \-\-user
Display the username for each line.
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-date
Display the modification timestamp for each line.
.TP
.BR \-L " " \fIRANGE\fR ", " \-\-line\-range " " \fIRANGE\fR
Filter annotation output to a specific line range (e.g. \fB10,50\fR).
.TP
.BR \-q ", " \-\-quiet
Suppress depot file header information.
.RE

.TP
.BR branch ", " br
List, create, or delete Perforce streams, translating Git branch workflows.
.RS
.TP
.BR \-a ", " \-\-all
List all depot streams on the Perforce server.
.TP
.BR \-d " " \fISTREAM\fR ", " \-\-delete " " \fISTREAM\fR
Delete the specified stream specification.
.TP
.BR \-P " " \fIPARENT\fR ", " \-\-parent " " \fIPARENT\fR
Specify the parent stream path when creating a new child stream.
.TP
.BR \-t " " \fITYPE\fR ", " \-\-type " " \fITYPE\fR
Stream type: \fBdevelopment\fR, \fBrelease\fR, \fBmainline\fR, \fBvirtual\fR, or \fBtask\fR.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Display verbose stream metadata.
.RE

.TP
.BR switch ", " sw
Switch the client workspace to a target Perforce stream. See \fBgfp\-switch\fR(1).
.RS
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-create
Create a new stream specification before switching to it.
.TP
.BR \-l ", " \-\-list
List all streams available for switching.
.TP
.BR \-P " " \fIPARENT\fR ", " \-\-parent " " \fIPARENT\fR
Specify parent stream when creating a new stream.
.TP
.BR \-t " " \fITYPE\fR ", " \-\-type " " \fITYPE\fR
Specify stream type when creating a new stream (default: \fBdevelopment\fR).
.TP
.BR \-s ", " \-\-stash
Automatically shelve open workspace changes before switching and unshelve after switching completes.
.RE

.TP
.BR clone
Clone a depot path or stream into a new directory, create a dedicated Perforce client workspace with Git-like options (\fBallwrite clobber nocompress unlocked\fR), and sync depot files.
.RS
.TP
.BR \-c " " \fICLIENT\fR ", " \-\-client " " \fICLIENT\fR
Name of the Perforce client workspace to create (defaults to \fIuser\fR_\fIdir\fR).
.TP
.BR \-d " " \fIDIR\fR ", " \-\-dir " " \fIDIR\fR
Target directory to clone into.
.RE

.TP
.BR reopen
Move opened files between changelists (e.g. from the default changelist to a numbered pending changelist).
.RS
.TP
.BR \-c " " \fICL\fR ", " \-\-cl " " \fICL\fR
Target changelist ID, or \fBdefault\fR.
.RE

.TP
.BR restore
Restore working tree files or discard/delete pending changelists.
.RS
.TP
.BR \-k ", " \-\-keep
Keep disk modifications intact when reverting changelist files.
.TP
.BR \-s ", " \-\-staged
Unstage files from changelists while preserving working tree changes on disk (\fBp4 revert \-k\fR).
.TP
.BR \-c " " \fICL\fR ", " \-\-cl " " \fICL\fR
Specify pending changelist ID to revert, delete server-side shelves, and purge atomically.
.TP
.BR \-f ", " \-\-force
Force revert of files or discard of changes.
.TP
.BR \-W ", " \-\-worktree
Discard local modifications in the working tree.
.RE

.TP
.BR resolve
Resolve conflicts between local workspace modifications and depot revisions (\fBp4 resolve\fR).
.RS
.TP
.B \-\-ours
Accept workspace revision and ignore conflicting depot edits (\fBp4 resolve \-ay\fR).
.TP
.B \-\-theirs
Accept depot revision and overwrite local workspace edits (\fBp4 resolve \-at\fR).
.TP
.B \-\-am
Automatically resolve non-conflicting changes (\fBp4 resolve \-am\fR).
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-dry\-run
Preview resolution actions without modifying files.
.RE

.TP
.BR rebase
Rebase, squash, or interactively manipulate pending changelists.
.RS
.TP
.BR \-s " " \fISOURCE_CL\fR ", " \-\-squash " " \fISOURCE_CL\fR
Source pending changelist to merge/squash into the target changelist.
.TP
.BR \-\-onto " " \fITARGET_CL\fR
Target pending changelist receiving the reopened files.
.TP
.BR \-i ", " \-\-interactive
Interactively select pending changelists to reorder, squash, or drop.
.TP
.BR \-m " " \fIMESSAGE\fR ", " \-\-message " " \fIMESSAGE\fR
New commit description for the combined changelist.
.RE

.TP
.BR completion
Output shell completion script for Bash, Zsh, or TCSH.
.RS
.TP
.I shell
Target shell format: \fBbash\fR, \fBzsh\fR, or \fBtcsh\fR.
.RE

.SH ENVIRONMENT VARIABLES
.TP
.B P4PORT
The host and port of the Perforce Helix Core server (e.g. \fBperforce:1666\fR). If unset, resolved via \fBp4 set\fR or \fBp4 info\fR.
.TP
.B P4USER
The Perforce username. If unset, resolved via \fBp4 set\fR, \fBp4 info\fR, or the system \fBUSER\fR variable.
.TP
.B P4CLIENT
The Perforce client workspace name. If unset, resolved via \fBp4 set\fR or \fBp4 info\fR.
.TP
.B GFP_SUBMIT_QUEUE_URL
HTTP/HTTPS URL of the Jenkins Gated Submit Queue validation job. Used by \fBgfp push\fR to report verification queue progress.
.TP
.B GFP_PUSH_MODE
Default submit behavior for \fBgfp push\fR. Set to \fBdirect\fR to default to direct depot submission (\fBp4 submit\fR), or \fBgated\fR (default) for pre-commit CI validation.
.TP
.B GFP_COMMAND
Exported by \fBgfp\fR to lifecycle hooks, containing the active subcommand name (e.g. \fBcommit\fR).
.TP
.B GFP_HOOK_STAGE
Exported by \fBgfp\fR to lifecycle hooks, containing either \fBpre\fR or \fBpost\fR.
.TP
.B GFP_WORKSPACE_ROOT
Exported by \fBgfp\fR to lifecycle hooks, containing the absolute filesystem path of the workspace root.
.TP
.B GFP_ARGS
Exported by \fBgfp\fR to lifecycle hooks, containing the raw arguments passed to the subcommand.

.SH CONFIGURATION FILES
.B gfp
loads configuration files hierarchically, merging global settings with workspace-specific overrides:

.IP 1. 4
\fB~/.gfp/config.json\fR (User-global configuration)
.IP 2. 4
\fB<workspace_root>/.gfp/config.json\fR (Workspace-local configuration)
.IP 3. 4
\fB~/.gfp/aliases.json\fR and \fB<workspace_root>/.gfp/aliases.json\fR (Custom command aliases)
.IP 4. 4
\fB~/.gfp/plugins.json\fR and \fB<workspace_root>/.gfp/plugins.json\fR (Declarative external commands)

.SS Configuration JSON Schema Example
.nf
{
    "submit_queue_url": "http://ci.corp.local/job/gfp-submit-queue/",
    "push_mode": "gated",
    "aliases": {
        "stc": "status -c",
        "ci-all": "commit -a",
        "review": "push --dry-run"
    }
}
.fi

.SH LIFECYCLE HOOKS
.B gfp
provides Git-like lifecycle hook automation. Hook scripts can be written in any executable scripting language (Bash, Python, etc.) and placed in either:
.IP \(bu 2
\fB<workspace_root>/.gfp/hooks/\fR (workspace-scoped hooks)
.IP \(bu 2
\fB~/.gfp/hooks/\fR (user-global hooks)

.SS Hook Naming Convention
Hooks follow the convention \fIstage\fR\fB\-\fR\fIcommand\fR or \fIstage\fR\fB_\fR\fIcommand\fR:
.TP
.BR pre\-commit ", " pre_commit
Executed before creating a pending changelist. If the script exits with a non-zero exit code, changelist creation is aborted immediately.
.TP
.BR post\-commit ", " post_commit
Executed after a changelist is successfully created.
.TP
.BR pre\-push ", " pre_push
Executed before submitting or shelving a changelist.
.TP
.BR post\-push ", " post_push
Executed after a changelist is successfully submitted or shelved.

.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B Clone a Perforce stream into a new Git-like workspace:
.nf
$ gfp clone //stream/main my-project
$ cd my-project
.fi

.TP
.B Check workspace status:
.nf
$ gfp status
.fi

.TP
.B Stage files and create a pending changelist:
.nf
$ gfp add src/main.py
$ gfp commit -m "feat: add entrypoint pipeline"
.fi

.TP
.B Diff local modifications against the depot:
.nf
$ gfp diff --stat
$ gfp diff
.fi

.TP
.B Shelve working changes (stash):
.nf
$ gfp stash save -m "WIP: refactoring parser"
$ gfp stash pop
.fi

.TP
.B Submit changes to depot:
.nf
# Via Jenkins gated submit queue (default)
$ gfp push

# Direct submit to depot (bypassing CI gate)
$ gfp push -f
.fi

.TP
.B Switch streams with auto-stashing:
.nf
$ gfp switch -s //stream/dev-feature
.fi

.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
General error (e.g. invalid arguments, missing executable, Perforce command failure).
.TP
.B >1
Hook failure exit code or Perforce exit code propagated to the caller.

